---
title: Lab 4.2 - Async Patterns and Best Practices
---

flowchart TD
    A[Async Operation] --> B{Exception Occurs?}

    B -->|Yes| C[Exception Handling]
    B -->|No| D[Normal Completion]

    C --> E[try/catch in async method]
    C --> F[AggregateException from Task.WhenAll]

    D --> G[Cancellation Check]
    G --> H{Cancelled?}
    H -->|Yes| I[OperationCanceledException]
    H -->|No| J[Continue Operation]

    subgraph "Cancellation Patterns"
        K[CancellationTokenSource] --> L[cts.Cancel()]
        L --> M[Token.ThrowIfCancellationRequested]
        M --> N[Cooperative Cancellation]

        O[CreateLinkedTokenSource] --> P[Parent + Child Tokens]
        P --> Q[Cancel via Parent Token]
    end

    subgraph "Timeout Patterns"
        R[CancellationTokenSource with Timeout] --> S[Auto-cancel after timespan]
        T[Task.WhenAny + Task.Delay] --> U[Manual timeout handling]
    end

    subgraph "Retry Patterns"
        V[Operation Fails] --> W[Retry with Backoff]
        W --> X[Exponential Delay]
        X --> Y[Max Retries Check]
        Y -->|Under Limit| V
        Y -->|Exceeded| Z[Fail Permanently]
    end

    subgraph "Progress Reporting"
        AA[IProgress&lt;T&gt;] --> BB[Report Method]
        BB --> CC[UI Updates]
        CC --> DD[Progress Callbacks]
    end

    subgraph "Async Lazy"
        EE[First Access] --> FF[Initialize Task]
        FF --> GG[Cache Result]
        HH[Subsequent Access] --> II[Return Cached Task]
    end

    subgraph "Common Pitfalls"
        JJ[async void] --> KK[Unhandled Exceptions]
        LL[.Result / .Wait()] --> MM[Deadlocks]
        NN[Multiple Threads] --> OO[Context Issues]
    end